WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
The Bird and the Whale

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:08.110
(An original tale by TheFableCottage.com)

3
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.550
Once there was a bird who fell in love with a whale.

4
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:17.540
And a whale who fell in love with a bird.

5
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.080
The bird loved the whale's beautiful smile.

6
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.650
He loved the way she swam through the water so gracefully.

7
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.050
The whale loved the bird's handsome white feathers.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.860
She loved to watch him soar through the sky.

9
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.110
And they both loved to eat lots of tiny fish.

10
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.530
All summer, the bird and the whale met in the bay.

11
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.260
They talked and talked.

12
00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:53.620
They talked about the moon, and the stars,

13
00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.460
and the ships on the ocean.

14
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.350
The bird told jokes and made the whale laugh.

15
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.660
The whale sang beautiful songs that made the bird cry

16
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.470
(even though he didn't know why).

17
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.300
"One day, you could meet my family in the ocean," said the whale.

18
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.280
"And you could meet my friends on the land," said the bird.

19
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.070
Everything was perfect.

20
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.400
But the world does not stop turning just because a bird and whale fall in love.

21
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.850
Summer turned into autumn,

22
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.320
and autumn turned into winter.

23
00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.930
The ocean turned cold,

24
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:39.050
and all the other whales left for warmer waters.

25
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.930
"Come with me to warmer waters," said the whale.

26
00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.220
"It’s a wonderful place.

27
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.440
It's always warm, and there are so many fish to eat."

28
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.340
"I love to eat fish," said the bird.

29
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.220
"And I love you. I will follow you anywhere.

30
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.750
But first, teach me to be a whale?"

31
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.760
"Like this!" said the whale, "follow me!"

32
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.670
and she dived deep into the water.

33
00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.620
"OK!" said the bird,

34
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.750
and he also dived deep into the water.

35
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.770
Deeper and deeper he went.

36
00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:24.940
"I'm swimming!" he laughed.  "I'm a whale!"

37
00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.640
But soon he couldn't breathe.

38
00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.800
He returned to the surface, gasping.

39
00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:34.800
He tried and tried and tried again,

40
00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.800
but he ran out of breath every time.

41
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.270
"I don't think a bird can become a whale," said the bird.

42
00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.260
"Come with me instead!

43
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.460
I live up on the cliffs. It's a wonderful place.

44
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:54.400
It's warm and cosy, and every morning you can watch the sun rise."

45
00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:58.500
"I love to watch the sun rise," said the whale.

46
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.590
"And I love you. I will follow you anywhere.

47
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.640
But first, teach me to be a bird?"

48
00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.090
"Like this!" said the bird. "Follow me!"

49
00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:14.020
and he flapped his wings and soared into the sky.

50
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.930
"OK!" said the whale.

51
00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:22.310
She squeezed her eyes shut and flapped her fins, just like the bird.

52
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.750
She flapped and flapped, up and down.

53
00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.840
Water splashed everywhere!

54
00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:34.250
"I'm flying!" she laughed. "I'm a bird!"

55
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.990
But when she opened her eyes, she wasn't soaring in the sky.

56
00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.190
She was still in the water.

57
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.430
She tried and tried and tried again,

58
00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.750
but she could not fly.

59
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.560
"I don't think a whale can become a bird," said the whale.

60
00:03:53.100 --> 00:04:00.190
"But if you can't fly, and I can't swim, where can we live together?" said the bird.

61
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:06.010
"We will stay here — in the waves!" said the whale.

62
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.000
But the bird shook his head sadly.

63
00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.310
"You love to swim deep in the ocean," he said.

64
00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.950
That is your favourite thing to do.

65
00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.960
You would never be happy here."

66
00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.190
The whale sighed.

67
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.990
"And you love to fly and soar into the sky," she said.

68
00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.620
"That is your favourite thing to do.

69
00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.620
You would never be happy here either."

70
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:38.310
And so, because the bird and whale loved each other so much,

71
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.300
they said goodbye.

72
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.360
But they never forgot each other.

73
00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:49.770
Every time the whale saw a bird flying high in the sky,

74
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.070
she thought of her bird.

75
00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.000
She hoped he was enjoying the skies — just like that.

76
00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.260
And every time the bird saw a whale diving deep in the ocean,

77
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.970
he thought of his whale.

78
00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.860
He hoped she was enjoying the ocean —

79
00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.510
— just like that.
